      "id": "text_4_9935",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "\u2705 Fixes applied in v2",
      "fontSize": 18,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "baseline": 18,
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "\u2705 Fixes applied in v2",
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "x": 1460,
      "y": 70,
      "width": 410.13,
      "height": 303.75,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#664500",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 186699714,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 1268073013,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1700000000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "id": "text_5_7912",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "1. club.password -> passwordHash\n   bcrypt-hashed before save, never returned by\n   any query.\n\n2. Removed the \"Message read by\" collection.\n   Read receipts are now DERIVED from\n   userClubSettings.lastReadMessageId instead\n   of one row per message per member.\n   -> O(1) write per read, not O(members).\n\n3. IDs: Mongo default ObjectId everywhere,\n   except Messages, which use a client-generated\n   UUID (stored as Binary subtype 4, not string)\n   so the client can render optimistic \"sending\"\n   state before the server round-trip.\n\n4. Messages.status no longer includes \"sending\" \u2014\n   that state is client-only, never persisted.",
      "fontSize": 13.5,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "baseline": 13.5,
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. club.password -> passwordHash\n   bcrypt-hashed before save, never returned by\n   any query.\n\n2. Removed the \"Message read by\" collection.\n   Read receipts are now DERIVED from\n   userClubSettings.lastReadMessageId instead\n   of one row per message per member.\n   -> O(1) write per read, not O(members).\n\n3. IDs: Mongo default ObjectId everywhere,\n   except Messages, which use a client-generated\n   UUID (stored as Binary subtype 4, not string)\n   so the client can render optimistic \"sending\"\n   state before the server round-trip.\n\n4. Messages.status no longer includes \"sending\" \u2014\n   that state is client-only, never persisted.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
